{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:4b1831f209ff85fb","name":"GR-75 Medium Transport","source":{"id":"source:reference-4b1831f209ff85fb","title":"GR-75 Medium Transport","revision":18711,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:36:09Z","sha256":"4d79b39da42d0f91e957b1e6548f7106c7e778ffba29cbecddb28e50690bb9f9","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18711","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=GR-75%20Medium%20Transport&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-4b1831f209ff85fb","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The New Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_New_Republic","referenceId":"reference:e6046dbb57e5abb0"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Though numerous transport ships are employed across the galaxy, the Gallofree Yards Transport is one of the most ubiquitous and often-used. It is a sleek-looking vessel, especially considering its size, but its outward appearance bellies its slow and ponderous nature. The ships can be used as freighters, but due to their low speed are most often used as short-range transports, moving goods and passengers from planet to planet, planet to station, or star system to star system.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["During ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", the GR-75 was popular with the Republic Navy as a resupply craft. Large numbers of the transports were used to supplement the Republic's extensive supply lines, enabling those lines to be stretched thin without significant interruption to the flow of goods to the front. A scant few were modified with improved shields and heavy weaponry and used to lure unwary pirates to their doom.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," wound down and the rise of the Empire began, many of these venerable transports found themselves in the employ of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"},". Following the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Endor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Endor"},", many GR-75s were modified into salvage ships. They became integral to the New Republic's initial campaigns against ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Imperial Remnant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Imperial_Remnant"},", because parts and equipment salvaged from long-dead ships were valuable commodities.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["In its stock configuration, the GR-75 Medium Transport is utilitarian and unexciting. Equipped with a large cargo hold and precious little in the way of defensive systems, it is a sitting duck on the space lanes unless accompanied by an escort. Its sublight drive and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," are slow, and it maneuvers like a sick bantha. The ship is relatively easy to modify, however, given the appropriate parts and mechanical expertise.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The GR-75s used by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"}," are often equipped with upgraded weaponry, shields, and engines. Internal systems are often rearranged, giving each GR-75 a unique floor plan depending on its specific function. Most often, the GR-75 is utilized to move troops and material. Others are modified to serve as hospital ships, landing craft, or salvage vessels. Regardless of its specific function, the GR-75 rarely looks different from the outside.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["GR-75 Medium Transport Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal (Frigate) ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -5; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 14 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 14), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 34; +14 Armor\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 400; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 15; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shield Rating"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shield_Rating"},": 45; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 134\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," Fly 12 Squares 